INSERT INTO `quest_offer_reward` (`ID`, `Emote1`, `Emote2`, `Emote3`, `Emote4`, `EmoteDelay1`, `EmoteDelay2`, `EmoteDelay3`, `EmoteDelay4`, `RewardText`, `VerifiedBuild`) VALUES
(41634, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Simply marvelous. A job well done. Thronda should listen well and follow your example. She has great potential, but her lack of discipline is a dire thorn in my side - and hers, too. Still, I can only partially blame her, for it is my sworn duty to her parents to foster her magical talent as much as her growth as a person.$B$BYou have my deepest gratitude, good traveler. Before you go, take one of these as compensation for the troubles. Be sure to step wary during these trying times.', 0),
(41635, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Is it done? Is this the head of their mongrel leader? Good riddance to them, their lot has chosen what path to tread - a path leading to their timely demise. I appreciate your courage, adventurer. Here, take this as reward for the good deed. With your actions, we may soon live our solemn lives yet again.', 0),
(41636, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'The crate from Mister Melain! I had met him on my short trip to Ambershire when I gathered the children for school, he told me what happened. Shocking that there are faithless heathens stealing from those who have already been dealt a bad hand by fate. The Light will shine upon you with benevolent rays for your heroic deed, good $C.', 0),
(41637, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Wonderful, their delighted expressions cast a smile on my own face everytime I see them. These children are the future of the Alliance, and it is our responsibility to prepare them for their own decisions as best as we possibly can. I will make sure the Church knows about your contributions today, good deeds will not go unnoticed. Did you learn something yourself, by chance? The island of Balor is a divisive topic within the kingdom, many of the superstitious dare not mention its name still. Regardless, it is part of our past and as such should be remembered.', 0),
(41638, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Oh, mother... I am so sorry to have left you in that lightforsaken place. Be rest assured, you will find a new resting place in Stormwind, my new home. Thank you - $N was it? With mother\'s ashes returned, I will deliver them to the Church before continuing my duties here with Sister Argent. Farewell, kind soul. May the blessing of the Light shine your way.', 0),
(41639, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<The witch is cackling in an uncomfortable manner.>$B$BUseful after all. Here, some homebrewed potions of mine, just for you. You may stay a while and ask me anything. The woods have knowledge most don\'t dare to ask...', 0),
(41642, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'What a tragedy, Christoph was a truly good-hearted man and father. Seeing him succumb to such a senseless death breaks my heart. But what about poor, poor Arnold? I fear for him, now that he is orphaned. Please, let me take care of how to tell him of his father\'s fate. The revered sister at the church of Ambershire will know what to say.$B$BThank you, kind soul. You\'ve done a good deed today. May the blessing of the Light shine your way.', 0),
(41643, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Interesting. With the testimonies you\'ve presented and my own information, we should be able to pinpoint potential suspects. Well done.', 0),
(41644, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'This is troubling news. Not only does it confirm VanCleef\'s schemes to run on a much grander scale, but we have to rule out the Defias being behind the rampant kidnappings. Leaving us to pursue a more grueling lead...', 0),
(41645, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Again, a dead lead. We\'re running out of options, deputy.', 0),
(41646, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Operative Hawthorne lets out a deep sigh hearing your findings. Looking clearly exhausted, he begins rubbing his eyes as a sign of defeat.>$B$BThis whole ordeal proves to be more of a conundrum than I had hoped it would be. All three suspects act unrelated to our case, setting us back to zero. As much as it dismays me, I have to start my investigation anew. I will revoke your deputization; what you\'ve done for me saved me valuable time, but I cannot demand any more of you. If I am fortunate enough, then the SI:7 will send someone to support me here. Until then, I must focus on my work. Farewell, $N.', 0),
(41647, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<The old woman is stirring her cauldron, which violently bubbles exuding a most pungent odor.>$B$BWell, well, well. What do we have here? A lost sheep trying to find a place to rest?', 0),
(41648, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Oho, splendid, darling. The Widow\'s Frills are especially thick this season, if we didn\'t need them for now I would make a loveable stew out of them. They\'re quite delectable, perhaps you can try them yourself once all of this is over. And this comb you\'ve brought - it\'s from a young woman. Let us not tarry any longer. Now then, to mix this all together...', 0),
(41661, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'I hope the poor merchant was simply robbed and not beaten for blood—or worse. Alas, you have done your part, and for that, I am more than thankful. There is little I can offer, but take this. It was the last painting I did.', 0),
(41662, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Where the guards falter, the people shall provide. You have my gratitude, adventurer. A few coins for your trouble.', 0),
(41663, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Mike, what a sly old fox. The man carries one of the most mediocre names I have ever heard, yet his mind could outwit any other intellect.', 0),
(41664, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'That utter, disgraceful dog. Bah, who would think that the laughingstock of children could be up to no good? Sir "Ambercheeks" is bold.', 0),
(41665, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Duke Sherwood is a close friend; many times he has denied the use of servants. It warms my heart to think he would find one in you. My armory is humble, and these are trying times—at most, for your service, I can reward you with this.', 0),
(41666, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Ah, there you are! Thank you, thank you. I believe they were going to dismantle my stall if you hadn\'t shown up when you did. As promised—a free pack of Amberglaze Donuts and an extra coin as a tip.', 0),
(41667, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hey $N, is she still looking at me? Bah, that woman makes me so uncomfortable. Anyway, did you manage to get the horseshoes? Oh, thank the Light. Here, take this and be quick about it. And, just in case, don\'t show up during the tournament.', 0),
(41668, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hand them over; everything is ready. You may take an apple yourself for helping me out.', 0),
(41669, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Grandmother sent you, and she said that? Oh, I miss her dearly. I can\'t wait to try everything she sent me. I hear the donuts are very famous in Northwind. And I will treasure this toy from Mother forever. Thank you, adventurer. You have done me a great favor, and as Prince of Stormwind, I would reward you with something from our armory—if I could. Instead, I will give you this book I have from the Archbishop.$B$BDo come and tell me of your adventures sometimes; this palace is dull and boring. I could use a friend.', 0),
(41670, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Some would tell you there is no meaning in this—clinging to the dead, to the past, each day. Yet, these tombstones become mere decorations if the dead are forgotten. A grim fate, worse than death itself.', 0),
(41671, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'With this returned, so too does hope return. During the gospel this year, we will reconnect with those whose faith has dimmed, for that is exactly what they need amidst the chaos enveloping these lands.', 0),
(41672, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You have my deepest thanks. There is little I can offer, despite all that big talk. With no visitors from outside Northwind, the inn barely gets a drunk or two. So, I offer you a warm meal, and you may choose any room upstairs and call it your own for as long as you are in Northwind.', 0),
(41673, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Whoa, it really is the size of her head! She will love it. Thank you; I will not forget this favor.', 0),
(41674, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You have slain that many? Good! Their blood will nourish the soil, and the grapes that grow from it will bear the sweet taste of victory.', 0),
(41675, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Jerry came up with this? Not a bad idea. I gave the kid a hard time; I should go talk to him. Thank you.', 0),
(41676, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Without their leaders, the remaining orcs should return to their filthy lands.', 0),
(41677, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'I heard them blowing up from here. Great job, pick one of these.', 0),
(41678, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Good, here is your prize. May the Light smite you should you falter from its path.', 0),
(41679, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'What—reward? And here I was thinking you were here only for the thrill of adventure. Here, have some coin.', 0),
(41680, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Argh, uergh–WIGGLES!', 0),
(41681, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Fleshy return with smelly orc.$B$BWiggles carry back to master.$B$BSmelly lost this, fleshy keep.$B$BBye fleshy.', 0),
(41682, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You may keep that pouch, I no longer need it.', 0),
(41683, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'A job well done, and a reward well deserved.', 0),
(41684, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'So orcs were responsible after all; but not the Blackrocks. The way you described them doesn\'t match with any recent encounters we had with any of the orc clans, at least not the ones I can recall by memory. We will take this to Stormwind and have the headquarters tackle this.$B$BRegarding the girl... I will see to it to retrieve her body myself; I need to see this orc camp either way. Leave telling her mother to me, it is nothing that should fall to someone like you anyway.', 0),
(41685, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'So Hawthorne deputized you as assistant for his investigations in Northwind. Let me see what results you have to show.$B$B<Shaw takes a thorough look through Hawthorne\'s journal and an even more thorough read over the letter you have found at the orc camp. With a stern expression, he rolls the parchment and shows you the seal at the end of it.>$B$BThis is the seal of the Stormreaver Clan. This is an old orc clan we believed to have perished at the end of the Second War. I have read through this letter and what\'s inside matches with the kingdom\'s ailments: They issued the abductions of careless citizens, but turned their focus to Northwind for some unknown reason. Still, this is not the most alarming revelation about this whole ordeal. But first, a reward for your assistance.', 0),
(41687, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Wonderful, just retribution for trespassing into my lands, raiding Birkhaven and ruining my mining schedules! They\'ve got what they had coming for them! I must thank you. Here, choose something to your liking, someone of your caliber more than deserved it.', 0),
(41688, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'The horse feed! Lady Mildenhall informed me someone has been tasked in retrieving the lost sacks from the gnolls. Am I relieved to see it all safe and mostly undamaged. We were running short on our old supplies and just feeding these horses hay does not provide them enough energy for the taxing physical exercise they have to fulfill in the tournament. Thank you very much again! Lady Mildenhall gave me some coin for you once you\'ve finished her task, so please take it.', 0),
(41689, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<You approach the poor thing with slow and careful movements. Greens in hand, you lay them gently in front of its bill, before witnessing it nibbling on the strands of grass. Distracting it with the strong aroma and flavour of the herbs, you have ample time to administer the bandage to its wing. Now that the wound is secured and the little one is strengthened by the greens, it keeps staring at you with an endearing look on its feathered face.>', 0),
(41690, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You were lucky, given you did not know what you fed this poor thing. The plants you picked are called Noble\'s Pillow, infamous for their muscle numbing properties. They most assuredly helped ease its pain, yet there is still much to do if you want to save the little one.', 0),
(41691, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<The old hag grinds up the herbs in a mortar before mixing in the gooey ambersap. Stirring the ointment, she applies it onto a new bandage. Carefully removing the old one, another batch is spread over the little ducks wound, much to its dismay. With quick but delicate movements the witch wraps the bandage around its left wing, securing it in place.>$B$BThere, darling; this will help it recover very quickly. Defenseless creatures like our friend here rarely have such luck at meeting a kind soul like you. And judging by its behaviour, it recognizes your efforts just as much. Your actions formed a formidable bond today. Make sure to foster it greatly, as power lies deeply rooted in such connections.', 0),
(41712, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Griselda is reading the dusty letter carefully, so as not to rip its paper with an unmindful move. A bittersweet expression hushes across the face, her eyes showing mild shock, but not the kind brought upon by bad news. Instead, a smile whisks itself upon her lips.>', 0),
(41768, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Does Lord Amberwood employ lowly peasants now to deliver royal documents? To be expected, but that matters little now.$B$BBe that as it may, you\'ve done your assignment amicably. Still, my gratitude has limits. I have crucial information to analyze, so I would appreciate it if you would leave me to deal with the ailments of the kingdom in peace.', 0),
(41796, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Scarves from our father? Oh my. Now this is a bit embarrassing. He\'s always been on the softer side of things, a dreamer, you could say. Don\'t get me wrong, though. I appreciate it very much. Alessa and I grew up in Stormwind. Since we were very little back then, we don\'t have many memories of the time, but it still feels weird for us to be back here. Having something familiar from home will help us with the situation, for sure. For that, you have my thanks.', 0),
(41797, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'A letter from Avette? How is she? I heard Duskwood is a treacherous place nowadays, not safe for any of the common folk.$B$B<Barbara opens the letter and quickly glances over a few lines. While doing so, a chuckle escapes her.>$B$BI see I have nothing to worry about, how relieving. It\'s been too long since I\'ve heard from her and I was beginning to assume the worst. Once Northwind\'s troubles subside, I will pay her a visit. It is more than overdue. Here, take these few coins as thanks from me and Avette. Trust me, you did more than you think for the both of us. Stay safe on your travels, $N.', 0);
INSERT INTO `quest_request_items` (`ID`, `EmoteOnComplete`, `EmoteOnIncomplete`, `CompletionText`, `VerifiedBuild`) VALUES
(41634, 0, 0, 'How are your dealings with my tower faring?', 0),
(41635, 0, 0, 'Stay safe, adventurer. Northwind\'s hills are not meant to be drenched in the blood of the innocent.', 0),
(41636, 0, 0, 'Welcome to our humble church. Are you here to visit a lost one, or perhaps for silent prayer?', 0),
(41637, 0, 0, 'How are you faring? I hope the little rascals aren\'t too much to handle.', 0),
(41638, 0, 0, 'With the wars over, I thought Northwind may finally return to its peaceful roots. Maybe I have been too naive to think so.', 0),
(41639, 0, 0, 'You better not question what I need these for.', 0),
(41642, 0, 0, '<Mirabelle is lost deep in prayer.>$B$BO, Blessed Light, guide this lost lamb back into your fold. May his son not suffer the pain of solitude, may he be reunited with his kin and compatriots.', 0),
(41643, 0, 0, '<Operative Hawthorne is noting something down in his journal. With a stern expression of contemplation, he is lost deep in thought.>', 0),
(41644, 0, 0, 'The people of Northwind are wealthy. So far we haven\'t received any ransom demands, but I would not rule out the possibility of that happening sooner than later.', 0),
(41645, 0, 0, 'Our relationship to the Dark Iron is strenuous, to put it lightly. The Bronzebeard dwarves of Ironforge have a more... creative way to describe it.', 0),
(41646, 0, 0, 'If you wish to assist in driving out the main force from Northwind, a local marshal is conducting his own operation in the Plump Pumpkin. You can find it to the southeast at Grimmen Lake.', 0),
(41648, 0, 0, 'Now, now. Don\'t let me wait too much.', 0),
(41661, 0, 0, 'I miss holding a brush...', 0),
(41662, 0, 0, 'Dirt and gnoll spittle–I must burn these clothes.', 0),
(41663, 0, 0, 'More scrolls to read.', 0),
(41664, 0, 0, 'My shoulders feel heavy.', 0),
(41665, 0, 0, 'Approach messenger, let me have what you carry.', 0),
(41666, 0, 0, 'The people are literally rioting over the donuts...', 0),
(41667, 0, 0, 'I will wipe that smile off her face.', 0),
(41668, 0, 0, 'Ah, my poor Anduin.', 0),
(41669, 0, 0, 'You should speak to Miss Katrana or Bolvar, I am unable to say much.', 0),
(41670, 0, 0, 'No easy task, but a task all the same. May you walk with the Light.', 0),
(41671, 0, 0, 'The fire was yet another test of faith.', 0),
(41672, 0, 0, 'I am counting on you.', 0),
(41673, 0, 0, 'She seemed very excited at the sight of the pearl.', 0),
(41674, 0, 0, 'I wish they would never experience a day of peace.', 0),
(41675, 0, 0, 'Orcs, damn orcs. ORCS!', 0),
(41676, 0, 0, 'Is it done?', 0),
(41677, 0, 0, 'Need some flint and stone?', 0),
(41678, 0, 0, 'Have you the chalice?', 0),
(41679, 0, 0, 'I said charred bones, not coal.', 0),
(41680, 0, 0, 'Uergh?', 0),
(41681, 0, 0, 'Wiggles heard it! WOOSH–DONK–BONK!', 0),
(41682, 0, 0, 'Dwarves are disgusting pigs.', 0),
(41683, 0, 0, 'Spare no second.', 0),
(41684, 0, 0, '$N? What brings you to me? You found the ones responsible?! Tell me!', 0),
(41685, 0, 0, 'What purpose do you have with the SI:7?', 0),
(41687, 0, 0, 'Don\'t you dare return without being drenched in ash and blood.', 0),
(41688, 0, 0, 'Oh, Greetings. Apologies, but I can\'t really spend any time on chit chat. Many of the competitors need their horses ready for practice.', 0),
(41689, 0, 0, '<The round button eyes stare at you.>', 0),
(41690, 0, 0, 'Awfully busy today, wouldn\'t you agree?', 0),
(41691, 0, 0, 'Don\'t tarry too long, its condition won\'t hold up forever.', 0),
(41712, 0, 0, 'Can I help you with something?', 0),
(41768, 0, 0, '<Lady Prestor pays you no attention.>', 0),
(41796, 0, 0, 'Anything I can help you with? I need to prepare for the tournament, our opponents won\'t be easy to defeat.', 0),
(41797, 0, 0, 'How can I help you? Need to refill your quiver?', 0);
